    "notes": "MODEL: FCFE at cost of equity through the component engine, the house bank precedent (HBAN, NTRS, STT, NAB.AX). Routing table says residual income on tangible book; FCFE-at-CoE is used for consistency with the other US banks and because TFC book carries $18.3B goodwill+intangibles and AOCI swings, and the business is paying out >100% of earnings during the CET1 glide. Mapping: revenue = net interest income + noninterest income (XBRL InterestIncomeExpenseNet + NoninterestIncome; the CSV has no revenue tag for this bank). 'ebitda_margin' = (pre-tax income after provision for credit losses + SBC) / revenue; sbc_pct deducts SBC back out (house). D&A = 0 (immaterial, inside expense). 'capex_pct' = equity retained to fund balance-sheet growth = revenue growth x (tangible common equity / revenue ~1.94), i.e. the capital needed to hold CET1 flat as RWA grows. cash_tax_rate = effective tax rate (FY2026 guide ~14.5%, tax-credit investments; ramps to 17%). Flows are pre-preferred-dividend, so preferred stock ($5,411M carrying value at 2026-06-30) is deducted once in equity_bridge; deposits and bank borrowings are operating funding, so net_debt = 0. FY0 is TTM to 30-Jun-2026 so the flows start on the same date as the share count (H1-26 buybacks already out of the count). Base TTM revenue: FY2025 20,319 (14,423 NII + 5,896 nonII) - H1-25 9,886 + H1-26 10,417 = 20,850. TTM pre-tax 6,806 = 32.6% of revenue (34.2% incl. SBC add-back); Q2-26 run-rate 34.5%. last_fcf = TTM net income 5,470 (pre-preferred) as the FCFE proxy before retention -- OCF is not usable for a bank (deposit and trading flows).",
